From ed753377616811d6988f6fd4a0af22c29ed7b6e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nihal Kumar Gupta <nihal.gupta@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:18:47 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2312/2368] media: qcom: camss: Add Glymur compatible

Glymur's camera subsystem hardware is a functional subset of X1E80100.
TPG, CSID, VFE, CSID wrapper and ICC resources are shared; Glymur has
three CSIPHY instances versus X1E80100's four.

qcom,x1e80100-camss is not used as a fallback compatible since it is
already claimed by its own binding schema, causing a duplicate
compatible warning in the DT schema checker.

Signed-off-by: Nihal Kumar Gupta <nihal.gupta@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Bryan O'Donoghue <bod@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 09d6c30d3faeaeb376e550a1dda882a1928c8ce6)
(cherry picked from commit 6b71b98b70c0fa9591312681af79ba4db80be649)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 3f8ec6c1ae65ed2a33ebeea81f031e2ca82c582f..e35b057ef99400430ed2385f49f87a0f9d34a3dd 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -5820,6 +5820,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id camss_dt_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8550-camss", .data = &sm8550_resources },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,sm8650-camss", .data = &sm8650_resources },
 	{ .compatible = "qcom,x1e80100-camss", .data = &x1e80100_resources },
+	{ .compatible = "qcom,glymur-camss", .data = &x1e80100_resources },
 	{ }
 };
 
